---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/layout/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Focus Pet"
  description="The terms for downloading and using Focus Pet."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
      <a href="/" class="font-heading font-semibold text-text-secondary no-underline hover:text-accent-blue">
        &larr; Back to Home
      </a>

      <div class="mt-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold md:text-4xl">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-text-secondary">Last updated August 20, 2026.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8 text-text-secondary">
        <div>
          <p>These Terms of Service govern your use of Focus Pet.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            By downloading, installing, creating an account for, purchasing Focus Pro through, or otherwise
            using Focus Pet, you agree to these Terms.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">If you do not agree to these Terms, do not use Focus Pet.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Using Focus Pet</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pet is a desktop focus and productivity companion for supported Windows and macOS computers.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet provides tools intended to help you manage focus sessions, reduce distractions, track
            progress, and interact with Focus Pet's game and customization features.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Core Focus Pet features are available without purchasing Focus Pro. Certain features, including
            Deep Focus and other premium features identified in the application, may require an active Focus
            Pro entitlement.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet is provided as a productivity aid. We do not guarantee that Focus Pet will prevent every
            distraction, block every application or website, or operate identically with every application,
            browser, operating-system version, hardware configuration, or third-party service.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Application and Website Detection</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            During an active focus session, Focus Pet may determine which application is currently active on
            your computer.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            For supported browsers, Focus Pet may also determine the active website domain in order to
            evaluate the Allow List or Block List selected for your focus session.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            This functionality may use operating-system features such as Windows application APIs or macOS
            Accessibility APIs.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">Focus Pet uses this information to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>evaluate your selected focus rules;</li>
            <li>determine whether your current activity is focused, distracted, or restricted;</li>
            <li>provide Normal Focus and Deep Focus behavior;</li>
            <li>track focus-session progress;</li>
            <li>calculate rewards, streaks, and focus statistics;</li>
            <li>display relevant Focus Pet notifications or warnings.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Focus Pet does not use application or website detection to intentionally read:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>the contents of your files or documents;</li>
            <li>the contents of webpages;</li>
            <li>text entered into applications or websites;</li>
            <li>passwords or other credentials;</li>
            <li>private messages;</li>
            <li>keystrokes;</li>
            <li>screenshots;</li>
            <li>screen recordings.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet's website rules operate on domains rather than storing full browsing URLs as focus-rule
            history.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Some detection or enforcement functionality may depend on operating-system permissions, supported
            browsers, application behavior, or other technical limitations. Focus Pet does not guarantee that
            every application or website can always be detected, blocked, closed, or otherwise controlled
            successfully.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Normal Focus and Deep Focus</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">Focus Pet may offer multiple focus modes.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Normal Focus is intended to provide supportive focus tracking. Activity outside your selected
            rules may be treated as a distraction and may affect Focus Pet rewards or statistics.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Deep Focus provides stronger restriction behavior and may attempt to warn about, close, or
            otherwise enforce restrictions against applications or websites according to the features available
            on the operating system and the settings selected by the user.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Deep Focus is a Focus Pro feature unless otherwise stated in the application.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You remain responsible for saving your work and choosing appropriate focus settings. Although Focus
            Pet is designed to prefer safe and graceful behavior, certain enforcement features may close
            applications when enabled.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Do not rely on Focus Pet as the sole method of protecting important work, preventing access to
            applications, or enforcing time-sensitive restrictions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Accounts and Guest Mode</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">Creating a Focus Pet account is optional.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You may use Focus Pet in guest mode without creating an account. Guest-mode progress is generally
            stored locally on the device and does not use Focus Pet cloud backup.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">If you create an account, Focus Pet may provide features including:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>cloud backup and restore;</li>
            <li>account authentication;</li>
            <li>Focus Pro entitlement association;</li>
            <li>restoring supported progress and settings when you sign in on another supported device.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for
            activity performed through your account.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You agree to provide accurate account information and not to impersonate another person or attempt
            to access another user's account.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Single-Active-Device Account Model</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">Focus Pet accounts currently use a single-active-device model.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You may sign in to your Focus Pet account on different supported devices over time, but only one
            device may hold the active authenticated Focus Pet session at a time.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Signing in on another device may require you to choose whether to take over the active account
            session. If you do so, the previously active device may be signed out.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet does not currently promise simultaneous active use of the same account across multiple
            devices.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Cloud Backup</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            If you choose to use a Focus Pet account, supported game progress and settings may be backed up
            using Focus Pet's cloud services.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Cloud backup is intended to help restore supported Focus Pet data when signing in on another
            supported device.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Cloud synchronization and restore depend on network availability and third-party service
            availability. Although Focus Pet is designed to protect user progress, we do not guarantee that
            cloud synchronization will always be instantaneous, uninterrupted, or free from errors.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You should not use Focus Pet cloud backup as the only backup system for information that is
            independently important to you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Focus Pro</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pro is an optional paid upgrade that provides access to premium Focus Pet functionality,
            including Deep Focus and other features identified in the application.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Available Focus Pro plans, prices, billing periods, and included features are displayed at the time
            of purchase.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">Focus Pet may offer:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>monthly subscription plans;</li>
            <li>yearly subscription plans;</li>
            <li>lifetime or other one-time purchase options.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The plans actually available to you are the plans displayed in Focus Pet or during checkout at the
            time of purchase.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Payments and Stripe</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pro payments are processed through <strong class="text-text-primary">Stripe</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            When you purchase Focus Pro, Focus Pet may open Stripe Checkout in your web browser.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Stripe may collect and process payment information under Stripe's own terms and privacy policy.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet does not directly need to store your complete payment-card details in its own application
            database.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Stripe is responsible for payment processing and billing events, including applicable subscription
            payments, renewals, failed payments, cancellations, and payment-method management.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Recurring Subscriptions</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            If you purchase a recurring Focus Pro subscription, such as a monthly or yearly plan, the
            subscription will automatically renew according to the terms shown during checkout unless it is
            cancelled before renewal.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Your payment method may be charged at each renewal according to the price and billing period
            presented at purchase, subject to any changes permitted by applicable law and communicated as
            required.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can manage supported billing and subscription settings through the billing-management options
            provided by Focus Pet and Stripe.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Cancelling a recurring subscription generally prevents future renewal. Unless otherwise required by
            applicable law or stated at the time of cancellation, cancellation does not necessarily remove
            access immediately; you may retain Focus Pro access through the end of the period you already paid
            for.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Lifetime Purchases</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            If Focus Pet offers a lifetime Focus Pro purchase, that purchase is a one-time payment for the
            Focus Pro access described at the time of purchase.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            "Lifetime" refers to access for the supported lifetime of the Focus Pet product or service and does
            not guarantee that every current feature, operating system, third-party integration, or technical
            implementation will remain unchanged forever.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Failed or Past-Due Payments</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            If a recurring payment fails, Stripe may retry the payment according to its billing settings.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet may preserve access temporarily while a payment remains in a retry or past-due state, and
            access may later be limited or removed if the subscription becomes unpaid, expires, is cancelled,
            or otherwise no longer grants access.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Refunds</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Except where required by applicable law or otherwise expressly stated at the time of purchase,
            purchases are generally subject to the refund rules communicated through Focus Pet, Stripe, or the
            applicable purchase flow.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Nothing in these Terms limits any refund, cancellation, or consumer-protection rights that cannot
            legally be waived in your jurisdiction.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you have a billing question, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:help@tryfocuspet.com">help@tryfocuspet.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Changes to Focus Pro and Pricing</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We may change the features included in Focus Pro or the prices offered for future purchases or
            renewal periods.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Any changes will be handled in accordance with applicable law and any notice requirements that
            apply.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            A change to future pricing does not retroactively change the amount already charged for a completed
            purchase.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">Focus Pet relies on third-party services to provide certain functionality.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">These currently include:</p>

          <h3 class="mt-6 font-heading text-base font-bold text-text-primary">Supabase</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">Supabase is used for functionality such as:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>user authentication;</li>
            <li>cloud backup and restore;</li>
            <li>account/session coordination;</li>
            <li>Focus Pro entitlement information;</li>
            <li>server-side functionality supporting Focus Pro.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="mt-6 font-heading text-base font-bold text-text-primary">Stripe</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">Stripe is used for functionality such as:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>Focus Pro Checkout;</li>
            <li>payment processing;</li>
            <li>recurring subscription billing;</li>
            <li>one-time Focus Pro payments where offered;</li>
            <li>payment-method management;</li>
            <li>subscription management;</li>
            <li>Stripe's Customer Portal.</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="mt-3">
            Third-party services are governed by their own terms, privacy policies, availability, and technical
            requirements.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We are not responsible for outages, changes, or failures caused solely by third-party services
            outside our reasonable control.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Updates and Availability</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">We may update Focus Pet from time to time to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>add or remove features;</li>
            <li>improve reliability or security;</li>
            <li>support new operating-system versions;</li>
            <li>modify Focus Pro functionality;</li>
            <li>fix bugs;</li>
            <li>change the user experience.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Some updates may be necessary to continue using certain features.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">We may modify, suspend, or discontinue parts of Focus Pet where reasonably necessary.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do not guarantee that Focus Pet will remain compatible with every operating-system version,
            browser, application, device, hardware configuration, or third-party integration indefinitely.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Acceptable Use</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">You agree not to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>use Focus Pet for unlawful purposes;</li>
            <li>interfere with or attempt to disrupt Focus Pet's services or infrastructure;</li>
            <li>attempt to gain unauthorized access to another user's account or Focus Pet systems;</li>
            <li>misuse Focus Pet in a way that could damage, disable, overload, or impair the service;</li>
            <li>attempt to bypass payment, account, entitlement, or access-control systems;</li>
            <li>distribute malicious software through or in connection with Focus Pet;</li>
            <li>
              reverse engineer, decompile, or modify Focus Pet except where such restrictions are prohibited by
              applicable law.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Intellectual Property</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pet, including its software, design, artwork, graphics, branding, characters, text, and other
            original content, is owned by Focus Pet or its applicable licensors and is protected by applicable
